@startuml 07-seq-branch
!include _style.iuml
title Branches: fork, preview, merge

actor "Author" as au
participant "Author's\nMUPPET" as am
participant "Host\nmain" as main
participant "Host\n@sketch" as b1
participant "Server MUPPET\n(views)" as sm
actor "Reviewer" as rv

au -> am : propose an edit\n(or undo to an earlier point)
am -> main : fork at state vector SV
main -> b1 ** : create @sketch\nparent=@main, fork=SV
b1 --> am : branch @sketch ready
am -> b1 : XTXP ops on @sketch
rv -> sm : view @sketch
sm -> b1 : branch state
sm -> main : parent state
sm --> rv : onion skin (@sketch over main)\nand redline (who changed what)
rv -> sm : accept
sm -> main : merge @sketch
main -> b1 : request ops since SV
b1 --> main : ops
main -> main : replay into main\n(ops commute: mechanical)
main -> main : fan out to all peers
b1 -> b1 : stays as history

note over main, b1
  A branch is identified by its address.
  It records its parent and the point
  where it was forked. Going back in
  history, proposals and previews are
  the same mechanism.
end note
@enduml
